{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KZ.GLnResidues","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KZ.GLnResidues","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Adjoin.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Bilinear"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.casimirLeg_eq_flipP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.casimirLeg_eq_flipP","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/GLnResidues.lean#L235-L252","doc":"**The split Casimir on legs `i ≠ j` is the flip `P_{ij}`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.casimirLeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.casimirLeg","kind":"def","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/GLnResidues.lean#L231-L233","doc":"The split `𝔤𝔩_n` Casimir (trace form) on legs `i, j`: `t_{ij} = ∑_{a,b} E^{(i)}_{ab} E^{(j)}_{ba}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.legE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.legE","kind":"def","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/GLnResidues.lean#L227-L229","doc":"The elementary matrix `E_{ab}` acting on tensor leg `i` of `V^{⊗m}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.flipP_mul_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.flipP_mul_self","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/GLnResidues.lean#L224-L225","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.flipP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.flipP","kind":"def","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/GLnResidues.lean#L220-L222","doc":"The flip `P_{ij}` of the tensor legs `i` and `j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.permP_mul_self_of_mul_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.permP_mul_self_of_mul_self","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/GLnResidues.lean#L216-L218","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.permP_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.permP_one","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/GLnResidues.lean#L212-L214","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.permP_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.permP_mul","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/GLnResidues.lean#L208-L210","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.permP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.permP","kind":"def","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/GLnResidues.lean#L203-L206","doc":"The action of `σ ∈ S_m` on `V^{⊗m}`, `V = K^n`, as a matrix indexed by `Fin m → Fin n`\n(column `x` is the basis vector `e_{x ∘ σ}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.sum_two_quartic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.sum_two_quartic","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/GLnResidues.lean#L177-L193","doc":"Two involutions satisfying the braid relation `aba = bab` (the transpositions `(12), (23)` of\n`S₃`): their sum `Q` satisfies `Q⁴ + 4 = 5 Q²`, i.e. `(Q² − 1)(Q² − 4) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.sum_three_cube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.sum_three_cube","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/GLnResidues.lean#L151-L175","doc":"Three involutions permuted by conjugation like the transpositions of `S₃`\n(`ab = bc = ca`, `ac = cb = ba`): their sum `S` satisfies `S³ = 9 S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.aeval_smul_of_roots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.aeval_smul_of_roots","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/GLnResidues.lean#L129-L141","doc":"**Scaling the roots.** If `∏_i (S − m_i) = 0` then `∏_i (c S − m_i c) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.nonResonant_of_int_roots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.nonResonant_of_int_roots","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/GLnResidues.lean#L109-L127","doc":"**Non-resonance from integer roots and an irrational coupling.** If `A` is killed by\n`∏_i (X − m_i c)` with `m_i ∈ ℤ` and `c ∉ ℚ`, then `A` is non-resonant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.aeval_adL_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.aeval_adL_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/GLnResidues.lean#L100-L107","doc":"**Annihilator of `ad_A`.** If `∏_i (A − a_i) = 0`, then\n`∏_j ∏_i (ad_A − (a_i − a_j)) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.aeval_mulRight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.aeval_mulRight","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/GLnResidues.lean#L91-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.aeval_mulLeft","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.aeval_mulLeft","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/GLnResidues.lean#L86-L89","doc":"`L_A` and `R_A` are annihilated by every polynomial annihilating `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.aeval_sub_eq_zero_of_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.GLnResidues.aeval_sub_eq_zero_of_commute","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/GLnResidues.lean#L33-L84","doc":"**Two commuting operators annihilated by the same split polynomial.** If `x, y` commute and\n`p = ∏_i (X − a_i)` kills both, then `∏_j ∏_i (X − (a_i − a_j))` kills `x − y`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}